  data: {
    LLM: "Prioritize the Ace and 3. In Madrasso, these two cards alone account for 21 out of 30 point-value in a suit. If you have the Ace of Trump, you are the master of the table.\n\nThe Seven Switch: Don't always swap the 7 for the King or Knight indicator immediately if you want to hide your trump strength. However, if the indicator is the Ace or 3, swap it as soon as possible!\n\nPartner Lead-Deduction: If your partner leads a small Diamond, they likely have either the Diamond Ace or no trump. If they lead a Trump, they are 'draining' the opponents of high cards to protect their own 3s in side suits.",
    Player: "Prioritize the Ace and 3. In Madrasso, these two cards alone account for 21 out of 30 point-value in a suit. If you have the Ace of Trump, you are the master of the table.\n\nThe Seven Switch: Don't always swap the 7 for the King or Knight indicator immediately if you want to hide your trump strength. However, if the indicator is the Ace or 3, swap it as soon as possible!\n\nPartner Lead-Deduction: If your partner leads a small Diamond, they likely have either the Diamond Ace or no trump. If they lead a Trump, they are 'draining' the opponents of high cards to protect their own 3s in side suits.",
